---
title: Tater Tot Casserole
tags: midwest, midwestern, casserole
image: "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/tater-tot-casserole-index-659de3c8c2d1f.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.125xw,0&resize=1200:*"
servings: 8
time required: 1 hour 15 minutes
source: https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a46305536/easy-tater-tot-casserole-recipe/
prep time: 10 minutes
author: Francesca Zani
---

Preheat oven to 375°F.

Heat a #skillet{} over medium-high heat with @olive oil{2%tbsp}.

Add @yellow onion{1}(finely chopped), @garlic{4%cloves}(coarsely chopped), @kosher salt{}, and other desired seasonings. Cook, stirring constantly, until lightly browned, about ~{7-8%minutes}.

Add @ground beef{1.5%lb}, breaking up the meat with a spoon, and cook, stirring frequently, until browned and no longer pink, about ~{7%minutes}. Season with @kosher salt{}, @black pepper{}, and other desired seasonings.

Transfer the beef mixture to a #medium bowl{}.

Reduce heat to medium and melt @unsalted butter{2%tbsp}. 

Add @all-purpose flour{1%tbsp} and cook, whisking constantly, until the roux is bubbly and fragrant, ~{1-2%minutes}. 

Slowly add @chicken broth{3/4%cup}, then whisk constantly until the mixture simmers and thickens; there should be no lumps. 

Stir in @cream of mushroom soup{1%can}(10.5-oz). Rinse can out with some additional water or chicken broth to get all the contents out.

Add the beef mixture, @mixed veggies{12%oz}(frozen, at least with corn and green beans), @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}, @?yellow mustard{1%tsp}(optional), and @cheese{3%oz}(grated, cheddar ideally). Season with @kosher salt{} and other desired seasonings.

Pour the mixture into a #13" x 9" baking dish{}. Spread evenly with a spoon or spatula.

Top with @cheese{3%oz}(grated, cheddar ideally). 

Arrange @tater tots{1.5%lb}(about 72) in horizontal rows on top, leaving a small gap between each.

Bake the casserole until the center and edges are bubbling, ~{35-40%minutes}. Top with @?scallions{}(thinly sliced) for serving.